<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 6 June, from 1523 to 1984.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-i-of-sweden" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gustav-i-of-sweden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1523 CE <span class="tih-ago">503 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gustav Vasa is elected King of Sweden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Strängnäs the Swedish estates chose Gustav Eriksson Vasa, leader of the revolt against Danish rule, as king. He broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and laid the foundations of the Swedish state. The day is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>'s National Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1844 CE <span class="tih-ago">182 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Williams founds the YMCA in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A draper's assistant, George Williams, and eleven friends founded the Young Men's Christian Association to support young workers in the city. It spread worldwide.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1918 CE <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Marines attack at Belleau Wood</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American Marines launched costly assaults on German positions west of Château-Thierry. Three weeks of fighting helped halt the German drive on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1933 CE <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First drive-in cinema opens in New Jersey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard Hollingshead opened his 'Automobile Movie <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a>' at Pennsauken, near Camden. Drive-ins became a fixture of post-war American suburban life.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1944 CE <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allied armies land in Normandy on D-Day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">About 156,000 Allied troops landed by sea and air on the Normandy coast. The invasion opened the long-awaited second front against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1984 CE <span class="tih-ago">42 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexey Pajitnov completes the first version of Tetris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Working at a Soviet Academy of Sciences computing centre in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, Pajitnov finished his falling-block puzzle game. It became one of the best-selling video games in history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li></ol>
